Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 00:00:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(resources): resolve licensed native vanilla images

Servers can reference built-in Bedrock images without redistributing them.
The saved official Bedrock 1.26.51.1 Hive stack uses native bread, bucket
and potion images; bundled ViaBedrock vanilla packs supply definitions but
omit these pixels. Register the typed built-in resource provider and obtain
the matching official package through the selected account's existing
licensed asset cache.

ViaBedrock invokes acquisition on its resource-pack executor, so Store
licensing, downloads and indexing never block the Netty event loop. With
no selected account, return no additional layers and retain the core
baseline. Missing Store credentials, declined consent, canceled login and
failed optional downloads also return no licensed layers. These images
supplement server resources; unavailable licensing must not disconnect
the player during pack preparation. Keep native overlays bottom-to-top with exact path casing and
PNG/JPG/TGA variants. Export only images plus synthetic identity manifests
below the bundled definitions and all server packs; preserve higher-pack
extension precedence and isolate mutable pack pixels from the asset cache.

Synthetic tests cover no-account acquisition, native layer order, exact
case, extension replacement, server priority and independent pixel copies.
Licensed bytes, accounts and captures remain private.
